stion.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6e60d33c-60ad-599c-81ce-62b57d47844c" :question/math-academy-id "q-50351" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent line to the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta $, at $\\theta =\\pi $,  given that \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(\\theta )=\\frac{1}{\\theta }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\,{x}^{′}(\\theta )=\\frac{1}{\\theta }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use the rule for differentiating parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\theta )}{{x}^{′}(\\theta )}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the numerator and denominator at $\\theta =\\pi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(\\pi ) & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot 0+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi \\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi ,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\pi ) & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot (-1)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi \\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nHence, the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =\\pi } & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\pi )}{{x}^{′}(\\pi )} \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi }{\\left(-\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\right)} \\\\  & =\\pi \\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092764 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48fb4307-6ed3-5c9c-b575-3ba634b07a24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )-4{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330604} {:answer/id #uuid "4d66b536-d432-592f-a552-3d83dea6fff4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )+{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330653} {:answer/id #uuid "aed125a5-00ff-5286-9d0e-22a4dfe0b47e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331494} {:answer/id #uuid "bc622ef6-2ea5-5738-a6db-23a2ff317b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )+4{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331610} {:answer/id #uuid "c74a4616-57fa-5359-a03f-682fd7db8330" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )+2{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aed125a5-00ff-5286-9d0e-22a4dfe0b47e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331494} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a1ff240-3ade-5343-b0cf-fe6ee4dd31c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332268}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c1df0a62-d91d-5d2f-932b-891ad126ab27" :question/math-academy-id "q-51198" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the arc length of the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}+(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092769 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa8e4e8a-def8-59fd-9414-de793030f970" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090815} {:answer/id #uuid "e5512fb6-5f11-5936-a1b8-cbcc62637488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090816} {:answer/id #uuid "fb4ab1cc-66ca-5a08-92b0-c804fb64b50f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090817} {:answer/id #uuid "374ddbdb-88fe-5555-b5ef-a6df66c945a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090818} {:answer/id #uuid "76a19d5f-dda6-5003-a855-91a04667462f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090819}] :answer-field/id #uuid "02f148f3-9db9-5e43-a6b4-52cd9279fc96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090814}] :question/id #uuid "53ed96ef-9c9f-5ffd-b6cc-3db87a8bb3e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-5365" :question/problem "Evaluate the geometric series $∑_(n = 2)^(∞)8\\left(-\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^{n - 1}$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092782 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f13048d-a08c-5208-aa0d-b20206026846" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∑_(n = 1)^(4)3^{n - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090893} {:answer/id #uuid "af1d8bf5-84f1-52b0-8086-7eb6da0939e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∑_(n = 1)^(4)\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot 9^{n - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090894} {:answer/id #uuid "c0a7b101-b84e-5dcd-87bf-76623b4da455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∑_(n = 1)^(4)\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^{n - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090895} {:answer/id #uuid "117d48fd-619b-5bc0-8ad7-68db69396a02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∑_(n = 1)^(4)3 \\cdot 2^{n - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090896} {:answer/id #uuid "6f312cd6-9a5c-5f96-af11-e79370c86af0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∑_(n = 1)^(4)\\left(\\frac{1}{9}\\right)^{n - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090897}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9992427b-0665-560e-9e40-159d8a6c86f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090892}] :question/id #uuid "b69d18f0-9f30-5d38-8e20-c20c2024e7c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-67001" :question/problem "The geometric series $1 + 3 + 9 + 27$ can be written using sigma notation as"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092787 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8