{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091501} :answer-field/id #uuid "507a51a0-2f38-5b8b-a0e1-0fe341eed3c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091498}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "41fbb86c-53b6-5410-a547-305f18db5384" :question/math-academy-id "q-8828" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to $1$ decimal place?" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{2\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 5\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-2 & =0 \\\\ 5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{2}{5}\\right)=0.380\\,506…≈0.380\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $4$ decimal places. \n\nSince $0.380\\,5$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=0.380\\,5.$\n\nTo find the other solution in the given interval, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=0.380\\,506…+\\pi =3.522\\,099…≈3.522\\,1\n$$\n\nrounded to $4$ decimal places. \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈0.380\\,5\\cdot 3.522\\,1≈1.3\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092888 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05e2e080-3c1b-5c3d-826a-c4649c776f9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354704} {:answer/id #uuid "25019ab2-57d6-57f4-94d0-70955b245551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354975} {:answer/id #uuid "5087f04f-1a8d-50c3-9538-460bfde672a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355383} {:answer/id #uuid "5be543d7-dd87-5708-9c64-afae64f57bb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355475} {:answer/id #uuid "65173a57-b4d1-57eb-b568-86395fef6a05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355562}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65173a57-b4d1-57eb-b568-86395fef6a05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355562} :answer-field/id #uuid "934b6b43-47e6-57a0-a839-d889e84f32a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "40bdf0c4-a9af-5a19-bf92-60c84db76070" :question/math-academy-id "q-8876" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 3\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\sqrt{3} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right)=\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\nTo find the other solution, we subtract $\\pi $ from the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\pi =-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{5\\pi }{6},\\,\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}=-\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{36}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092910 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4e2083f-7994-5f95-9fcb-b43eff2eedc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(e^{-y/2} - e^{y/2})" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218