dent :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354923} {:answer/id #uuid "26c7e024-7766-5b8c-898b-5247732acaf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354989} {:answer/id #uuid "d0af74d7-a4fe-5d63-a786-980acc57c4d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356491} {:answer/id #uuid "e7f4d1e0-73ef-5ab0-a6f3-9d71508758c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7f4d1e0-73ef-5ab0-a6f3-9d71508758c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356691} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b0d2279-1848-5b7a-a647-c3be2dbb59d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b4116e5d-69c2-5e7a-a45f-c3940ca942d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-9446" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{2})=$" :question/worked-solution "The definition of $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{2}) & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{2}}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{2}}-{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1/\\sqrt{2})}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{2}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{2-1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092922 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "190a5314-e72d-527b-aa9e-4c0079dd688c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357971} {:answer/id #uuid "1bee1bb4-be7d-5d20-8d21-32d53d01088d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357991} {:answer/id #uuid "a7a0db5f-5c7a-5f5e-a290-e7a1248188e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359199} {:answer/id #uuid "be699b03-471d-5316-a2b6-92062d60c4b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359416} {:answer/id #uuid "efdd4d3d-453e-5e4d-8a75-09e728ac5829" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "190a5314-e72d-527b-aa9e-4c0079dd688c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357971} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a502992-4bc8-5b1f-9a6e-579818ef462a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360195}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dfaa6223-b113-5398-adeb-e8d8b6d36965" :question/math-academy-id "q-9532" :question/problem "![](images/08/085be1e624ae99afee256d2a9591f17d2f33f688364b6e59fdcd7c415206bda7.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the polar curve $r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{5\\pi }{6}$ (shown in blue in the diagram above)." :question/worked-solution "The arc length $L$ of a polar curve $r=r(\\theta )$ is given by\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\right)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6}1\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\theta {|}_{\\pi /2}^{5\\pi /6} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092923 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a7c6d33-ec9d-5f09-8a41-23c7079e0681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091742} {:answer/id #uuid "635d1f78-1ff1-548c-b1d2-727e82d8d662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531082} {:answer/id #uuid "ad493751-d3c8-5246-8a30-3a2a4aefa677" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531239} {:answer/id #uuid "b6a466dc-34ab-5292-b042-6078d2d70c1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-{e}^{-\\pi /2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531253} {:answer/id #uuid "d7923dd0-6a1a-51d5-bb60-8f501bdb44b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{e}^{\\pi /2}" :db/i